# Lychee ignore patterns - regex patterns for URLs to skip during link checking

# Localhost and local development URLs
https?://localhost
https?://127\.0\.0\.1

# Example and placeholder URLs used by the template
https?://example\.com
https://docs\.rs/example-sum-package-name

# Web Archive rejects automated checks despite serving browser requests
https://web\.archive\.org

# These pages require a browser session or reject automated HEAD/GET probes.
https://openai\.com/index/introducing-gpt-oss/
https://openai\.com/index/introducing-simpleqa/
https://openai\.com/policies/eu-terms-of-use/
https://openai\.com/policies/services-agreement/
https://artofproblemsolving\.com/wiki/index\.php/AIME_Problems_and_Solutions
https://app\.docker\.com/settings/personal-access-tokens

# The European Commission's digital-strategy site answers GitHub's runner
# address space with 403 while serving the same URL normally elsewhere. Run
# 33968819188 rejected
# `/en/policies/guidelines-gpai-providers` (LEGAL-COMPLIANCE.md:359) with
# `Rejected status code: 403 Forbidden`; the same URL answers 200 from a
# workstation for GET and HEAD alike, under lychee's own user agent, under
# `curl/8.20.0` and under a browser agent -- so the refusal follows the caller's
# network, not its user agent, and the page is not broken. 403 is deliberately
# not in the workflow's `--accept` list, because elsewhere it does mean "gone",
# so the exception is named here instead. The Wayback fallback cannot rescue it
# either: `check-web-archive.mjs` found no snapshot.
https://digital-strategy\.ec\.europa\.eu/

# The HTML is stamped and served from src/web/, so this build-time relative
# asset is not resolvable from src/web/app/index.html in the checkout.
styles\.css\?v=__FORMAL_AI_ASSET_VERSION__

# GitHub issue and pull-request pages, which CI cannot verify.
#
# GitHub answers anonymous requests for these pages from CI address ranges with
# a flat 404 -- not a redirect, not a 429 -- so an unauthenticated checker
# reports every one of them as broken. On 2026-08-17 this was 500 of 533 errors
# here, and a `workflow_dispatch` run on `main` failed identically (488 of 523),
# so it is not specific to any branch. `rust-lang/rust/issues/1` also 404s
# anonymously from the same network, confirming the behaviour is GitHub-wide.
# The check had stayed green only because `--max-cache-age 1d` kept serving
# verdicts recorded before GitHub started refusing these requests.
#
# Passing lychee a GITHUB_TOKEN does not help: it was tried as both the action's
# `token:` input and the `env:` variable, and the 404s were unchanged, so lychee
# checks these by HTTP rather than through the API that does answer 200.
#
# The same refusal covers /blob/: `formal-ai/blob/main/LICENSE` 404s
# anonymously while the file plainly exists, so file-view links are skipped too.
#
# Scoped to the page types GitHub refuses. Bare repository URLs, /tree/ and
# /releases/ are still checked, so a mistyped or deleted repository is still
# caught.
https://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/(issues|pull)/[0-9]+
https://github\.com/[^/]+/[^/]+/blob/
